4. MANDATORY VISIBLE ATTRIBUTION

Every Deployment of the Software, whether modified or unmodified, must retain
visible, working attribution links to both of the following destinations:

(a) Kitgenix: https://kitgenix.com
(b) Original Hoplane repository: https://github.com/Kitgenix/hoplane

The attribution requirement applies to each HTML page generated or served by
the Software, including, where present, the public landing page, dashboard,
sign-in and setup screens, password-protection pages, redirect-warning pages,
link-preview pages and application-rendered error pages.

On each such page, the links must:

(a) be plainly visible and reasonably legible in the ordinary page interface;
(b) be clickable and lead to the exact destinations listed above;
(c) remain accessible to a person who can ordinarily view that page, without
    requiring an unrelated login, payment, or additional service; and
(d) not be concealed, disabled, obscured, deceptively labelled, or replaced
    by non-functional text or images.

The attribution may be restyled to match the Deployment's design and may appear
in a footer, sidebar or similar location. It need not retain the original
Hoplane styling or branding, so long as the required attribution remains clear
and functional.

Attribution is not required in HTTP redirect responses, JSON or other API
responses, machine-readable data, non-HTML content, or third-party error pages
not generated or served by the Software.

This requirement applies to modified Software, rebranded Deployments, and
Deployments offered as part of a commercial service.

